Camoufox: name Camoufox, not Mozilla, in the Windows version resources.

config/create_rc.py writes every exe's and dll's VERSIONINFO, defaulting to
CompanyName "Mozilla Foundation" and LegalTrademarks "Mozilla", and the
module.ver of camoufox.exe, private_browsing.exe and plugin-container.exe set
"Mozilla Corporation" and Firefox's trademark line. An unsigned file claiming
to be Mozilla's reads as an impersonation to antivirus. CompanyName now
defaults to MOZ_APP_VENDOR and the trademark line is empty; the copyright
still credits the Mozilla developers. None of this is visible to a page.

diff --git a/browser/app/module.ver b/browser/app/module.ver
index 5ef8d2a02a..333c1eb4b0 100644
--- a/browser/app/module.ver
+++ b/browser/app/module.ver
@@ -1,8 +1,6 @@
-WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Mozilla Corporation
-WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=©Firefox and Mozilla Developers; available under the MPL 2 license.
+WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=©Camoufox and Mozilla Developers; available under the MPL 2 license.
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION=@MOZ_APP_WINVERSION@
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION_STRING=@MOZ_APP_VERSION@
-WIN32_MODULE_TRADEMARKS=Firefox is a Trademark of The Mozilla Foundation.
 WIN32_MODULE_DESCRIPTION=@MOZ_APP_DISPLAYNAME@
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTNAME=@MOZ_APP_DISPLAYNAME@
 WIN32_MODULE_NAME=@MOZ_APP_DISPLAYNAME@
